swer/id #uuid "42531acf-e3b1-5ebf-b2e5-355551db3842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234648} {:answer/id #uuid "9cbea967-4af3-5a64-b6ab-5b69a3e7ef69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234786} {:answer/id #uuid "b3b9b3ae-2a50-574c-bc09-ca9bdcb3fe18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbea967-4af3-5a64-b6ab-5b69a3e7ef69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234786} :answer-field/id #uuid "a701d358-5fb9-58f4-9c4f-33c1160ac672" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df097f49-5d4b-56bd-b0e8-a7fcc926dc0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120254" :question/problem "![](images/68/6882323d2c8017e95100a0ab9d1091fdf149e884ef27d2d2bf59ab7609b1a960.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+2b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8309dc45ac43c6642010e744de5a062d6575d48ba85bd642df39dd261f47422.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =2b-2a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+2b=-2a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Scalar Factor When Direction Reverses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cdd0854-261d-5ed4-92ef-477febc75b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234639} {:answer/id #uuid "3eab765d-2302-5205-b5fd-0ada1e027409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234642} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5da092-7603-5a36-a455-4137459af1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234713} {:answer/id #uuid "dde73660-f588-5765-aec3-a2559c655608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234894} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2c8c3-d49b-55df-8a1c-5ef41ca2446f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2c8c3-d49b-55df-8a1c-5ef41ca2446f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234905} :answer-field/id #uuid "959370f5-d157-5592-9470-19e5d767b960" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "16c001cc-439d-56cc-834f-f6d6a747b8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-120257" :question/problem "![](images/55/551316d1e36175ca302c5c472d4109a9bc9cadf32cc85d2a1751424a386070cc.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a-2b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/40/40a0137d6227212db9b7ef9f349029838f3f51398790ec5e1c304e12c3743a0f.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{1}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-\\frac{1}{2}a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Scalar Factor When Direction Reverses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f9a6c9b-836b-5e25-9560-a76d555bd2ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234563} {:answer/id #uuid "511f739e-027e-56d9-a3e1-c31426592471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234671} {:answer/id #uuid "a66f9626-a549-5ae7-8d06-4cfb6ab29c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234795} {:answer/id #uuid "c1efac91-7f8d-5ea4-a7ef-83e55e07f3e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234848} {:answer/id #uuid "c74cfa2b-3621-5ace-b7aa-47f1de8073f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1efac91-7f8d-5ea4-a7ef-83e55e07f3e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234848} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe75fa5-1b4a-5d3