a+4b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Scalar Factor When Direction Reverses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1182f91c-63ce-5f01-9627-833009eb360a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234566} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef1d698-0ee1-57ea-847b-94501bb643d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234594} {:answer/id #uuid "7408ca41-bbb9-508a-9de3-c8047ac6e775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234723} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d28957-6426-5dac-b805-2b8ae5ac411e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234798} {:answer/id #uuid "f29e2e73-ee24-5a15-b5ab-0a41ed9f87a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1182f91c-63ce-5f01-9627-833009eb360a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234566} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7535fb-bd1e-5516-b397-b16df4487f2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c314517-ec65-5a1b-988c-5b9d35453290" :question/math-academy-id "q-367052" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1d424b5db0534a8d9abc9b0aa84dcb2e6860a7ed51de7390fc4f7e91c1c33f2b.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+4b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+4b.\n$$\n\nW