th} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234609} {:answer/id #uuid "c93d8a53-26a7-5744-b10b-5b8f0da3c405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234861} {:answer/id #uuid "da616d4e-0a1e-55df-a589-db736030d4b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234889} {:answer/id #uuid "e79cd088-e254-50a4-9040-d34103eae50a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c93d8a53-26a7-5744-b10b-5b8f0da3c405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234861} :answer-field/id #uuid "9706ed72-1b58-5bbe-8976-330e0740d99e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9d1dc6a-3cc4-5a49-870f-4f180b06cd63" :question/math-academy-id "q-70148" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3f77b108decdfe95fe06d1ace87ee7f844a4f937f8b67a9f14e750a09ae4d57.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a-b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/7f/7f29124776f69f370b3129313fd1c2fa850924f446c6f086dcacd170f1ca6d24.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2.5|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2.5a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-b-2.5a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-b=-2.5a-b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2.5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Scalar Factor When Direction Reverses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab5b44a-6f14-5d8c-b994-0ff723092bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234586} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5b4c72-e340-52b5-be53-6903f63361a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234611} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe36434-9519-583f-9b69-c587e4937715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234866} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1ea7c1-61ca-56ba-a7d9-91573e3d6a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234869} {:answer/id #uuid "f46ca5b6-1fd3-597e-9657-e4197a5f9d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab5b44a-6f14-5d8c-b994-0ff723092bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234586} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa48e98-a238-5102-8717-85e261cb4e21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adcdd06d-1586-51df-9df4-c005428c239d" :question/math-academy-id "q-77451" :question/problem "![](images/28/28faea3a553c505a8a5ab9bc7dd6e784dd23a47c336c70d31218fbe249d57cff.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+3b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+3b.\n$$\n\nWe 